8o9|n|That which is destitute of light or whiteness; the darkest color, or rather a destitution of all color; as, a cloth has a good black. ; A black pigment or dye. ; A negro; a person whose skin is of a black color, or shaded with black; esp. a member or descendant of certain African races. ; A black garment or dress; as, she wears black ; Mourning garments of a black color; funereal drapery. ; The part of a thing which is distinguished from the rest by being black. ; A stain; a spot; a smooch.	a:79h,72,1;2hhb,29,1;1eiw,1,2~1eiw,1,2;2hhb,29,1;79h,72,1	v:2hhb,29,1;1bj4,9,9~1bj4,9,9;2hhb,29,1	V:1acr,47,6;2gql,22,1;1h70,21,2~1acr,47,6;1h70,21,2;2gql,22,1	n:79h,106,10;1j0g,61,7;1n3c,26,2~79h,106,10;1j0g,61,7;1n3c,26,2	N:26pr,72,1;y7i,63,1;1nx1,63,1;zvq,55,5;20dt,55,1;w04,53,4;lkr,46,2;1u8j,41,1;939,41,4;9ne,40,17;118l,35,3;25xe,32,2;118k,32,3;2gql,32,2;1oae,32,10~1yxc,23,23;9ne,40,17;1oae,32,10;zvq,55,5;w04,53,4;939,41,4;118l,35,3;118k,32,3;6i0,1,3;1acr,31,2;95j,11,2;25xe,32,2;2gql,32,2;lkr,46,2;1n3c,26,2
